  ],
  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "H. maritima MH2T (DSM 10411) was grown mixotrophically in medium (DSMZ medium 854) containing 6.2 mM NH4Cl, 2.2 mM CaCl2·2H2O, 1.6 mM MgCl2·6H2O, 4.4 mM KCl, 2.4 mM KH2PO4, 427.8 mM NaCl, 14.3 mM MOPS buffer, 200 mg l−1 yeast extract, 1 mg l−1 resazurin, 10 g l−1 sulfur powder, 10 ml l−1 trace element solution out of DSMZ medium 141 and 1 ml l−1 Wolfe’s vitamin solution (20 mg l−1 biotin, 20 mg l−1 folic acid, 100 mg l−1 pyridoxamine dihydrochloride, 50 mg l−1 thiamine dihydrochloride, 50 mg l−1 riboflavin, 50 mg l−1 riboflavin, 50 mg l−1 dl-Ca-pantothenate, 1 mg l−1 cyanocobalamin, 50 mg l−1 4-aminobenzoic acid and 50 mg l−1 lipoic acid)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "First dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH, then add minerals. Adjust final to pH 7.0 with KOH."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "The medium was prepared without sulfur and vitamin solution, made anaerobic by bubbling with N2 (100%) and reduced by the addition of Na2S·9H2O to a final concentration of 0.05% (w/v)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "The pH of the medium was adjusted to 5.5–6.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": "The medium was dispensed anaerobically into serum bottles containing sulfur powder; the bottles were sealed with butyl-rubber stoppers and aluminium caps and autoclaved for 40 min at 110 °C."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "Before inoculation, the vitamin solution was added and the gas phase was replaced with the required quantities of H2:CO2 (60:40, 80:20, 95:5, 98:2 or 99:1) at 1 bar overpressure."
    }
  ]
}